{%- comment -%}
  wb-cart-label.liquid — the customer's label words as the headline of a basket line
  (drawer + cart page), Nov 2026 mobile review.

  The basket photo is the product's stock "YOUR TEXT HERE" mock, and the words the
  customer typed were two small grey "Label text:" / "Created by:" rows among the
  options — so the basket never said back the one thing they had personalised. This
  prints them first, larger:   "Happy 50th Dad" — Love from Jo

  Display only: nothing is added to the cart, and the properties that reach the order
  are unchanged. The caller skips the "Label text" and "Created by" rows in its
  property loop when this renders (see `wb_label_shown` below), so the words aren't
  shown twice.

  Usage, inside the item details, before the <dl>:
    {%- render 'wb-cart-label', item: item -%}
  and in the property loop:
    if property.first == 'Label text' or property.first == 'Created by' → skip
    when item.properties['Label text'] is not blank.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign wb_cl_text = item.properties['Label text'] | strip
  assign wb_cl_author = item.properties['Created by'] | strip
-%}
{%- if wb_cl_text != blank -%}
  <p class="wb-cart-label">
    <span class="visually-hidden">Label text: </span>
    <span class="wb-cart-label__text">&ldquo;{{ wb_cl_text | escape }}&rdquo;</span>
    {%- if wb_cl_author != blank -%}
      <span class="wb-cart-label__author"> &mdash; <span class="visually-hidden">created by </span>{{ wb_cl_author | escape }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}
  </p>
{%- endif -%}
